-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Background.Orthonormalization.Orthogonalization.PhiNorm` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). ### Cauchy–Schwarz for a positive functional
--
--   The module is vendored read-only from the `orthogonalization` development of [vidick/commuting-repetition](https://github.com/vidick/commuting-repetition) (Apache 2.0; commit and upstream path in the file header) by `scripts/vendor-repetition.py`.
--
--   **Triangle inequality** for the seminorm `‖·‖_φ` of tuples:
--   `‖b + c‖_φ ≤ ‖b‖_φ + ‖c‖_φ`.
--
--   The proof expands `‖b + c‖_φ²`, bounds each cross term by Cauchy–Schwarz for
--   `φ` and then sums with the discrete Cauchy–Schwarz inequality
--   `Real.sum_sqrt_mul_sqrt_le`.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open Orthogonalization
--   open scoped ComplexOrder BigOperators
--   variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]
--   variable {φ : (H →L[ℂ] H) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
--
--   theorem Orthogonalization.phiNormSq_add_le (hφ : ∀ z : H →L[ℂ] H, 0 ≤ φ (star z * z)) (b c : ι → H →L[ℂ] H) :
--       Real.sqrt (phiNormSq φ (b + c))
--         ≤ Real.sqrt (phiNormSq φ b) + Real.sqrt (phiNormSq φ c)
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** `Orthogonalization.phiNormSq_add_le` is declared in `MIPRE/Background/Orthonormalization/Orthogonalization/PhiNorm.lean`, lines 247–307. The binders, hypotheses and conclusion are exactly those of the Lean statement above; the uploaded statement elaborates to the same type as the declaration in the repository. The definitions it mentions are those of the published definition bundles of the module's import closure.
